---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import WikiSectionCard from '../components/WikiSectionCard.astro';
import WikiSectionNav from '../components/WikiSectionNav.astro';
import { GAME_FACTS, SITE } from '../data/site';

const path = '/characters/';
const title = 'Beast of Reincarnation Characters: Emma, Koo and Story Cast';
const description =
  'Beast of Reincarnation characters: Emma and Koo plus Brad, Kagura, Kunai, Shidou and Mikoto, with story roles, combat jobs and skill tree links.';
const image = '/images/beast-of-reincarnation-koo-blighted-wolf.webp';
const canonical = new URL(path, SITE.url).href;
// The Emma and Koo character pages were merged into this page on 2026-11-16; their URLs
// 301 here and keep #emma / #koo anchors.
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'CollectionPage', name: title, description, url: canonical,
    about: { '@type': 'VideoGame', name: GAME_FACTS.name, url: GAME_FACTS.source },
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: SITE.name, url: SITE.url },
    mainEntity: { '@type': 'ItemList', numberOfItems: 7, itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Emma', url: new URL('/characters/#emma', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Koo', url: new URL('/characters/#koo', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Brad', url: new URL('/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-brad/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 4, name: 'Kagura', url: new URL('/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-kagura/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 5, name: 'Kunai', url: new URL('/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-kunai/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 6, name: 'Shidou', url: new URL('/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-shidou/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 7, name: 'Mikoto', url: new URL('/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-mikoto/', SITE.url).href },
    ] },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Guides', item: new URL('/guides/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Characters', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} image={image} imageAlt="Koo, the blighted dog companion, in Beast of Reincarnation">
  <JsonLd slot="head" schema={schema} />
  <section class="border-b border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/30"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-5 text-xs text-ash-400"><a href="/" class="hover:text-ember-400">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-ember-400">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span class="text-ash-300">Characters</span></nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-ash-50 md:text-5xl">Beast of Reincarnation Characters: Emma, Koo and Story Cast</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash-300">Beast of Reincarnation is built around two playable partners: Emma's direct sword and movement tools, and Koo's commanded techniques and Bloom Arts. Below are both partners' systems and build advice, followed by the story cast.</p>
  </div></section>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <WikiSectionNav active={path} />
    <section id="emma" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="grid items-start gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_.9fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ember-400">Playable character</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold text-ash-50">Emma: skills, weapons and combat role</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ash-300">Emma is the direct-action half of the Beast of Reincarnation team. Her sword attacks, ranged weapons, Hair traversal and Entanglement tools determine how you create openings while Koo supplies techniques and Bloom Arts.</p>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/beast-of-reincarnation-emma-character.webp" alt="Emma, protagonist of Beast of Reincarnation, holding her sword" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border border-ash-800 object-cover" />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">Emma's main systems</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-ash-300"><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Weapons:</strong> Mechblade forms, named swords and the Spring Thunder Crossbow.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Movement:</strong> Hair abilities support Lift, Extend and air-assassination routes.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Skill trees:</strong> Entanglement Overdrive, Hair and Track Shot are the key paths documented by the cited progression guide.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Resources:</strong> Parrying feeds Emma's entanglement loop while also helping Koo.</li></ul></div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">Emma build advice without unsupported numbers</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ash-300">Start with the problem you are trying to solve. If Emma cannot escape, investigate the Track Shot roll and Hair movement paths. If a boss fight is too slow, compare the weapon element and the target's visible weakness before spending points. If the entanglement gauge is empty, practise the parry window instead of assuming a higher-damage weapon will fix the loop.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-ash-800">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><tbody>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800 first:border-t-0"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Role</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Playable protagonist, Blightborn – an outcast who carries the blight and travels west through a ruined Japan without her past memories or emotions</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Weapons</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">21 blades (Mechblades to Kanzashi), the Spring Thunder Crossbow and bows with elemental ammo</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Movement</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Hair-based traversal (Lift and Extend)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Japanese voice</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Yui Ishikawa, named in the June cast announcement (English voice not named – see the <a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/voice-cast-and-previews/">voice-cast page</a>)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Skill achievements</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Giant Tree Budburst (every Emma skill; the full tree is a level-100 goal) and Blademaster (fully upgraded Blade Arts and Finishers – some only open in New Game+)</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">How Emma fights</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-ash-300">
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Blades and Blade Arts:</strong> each blade has a passive (Shock, Poison, Acid, Flame, healing). Blade Arts and Finishers are earned from bosses – Blade Art: Dokuzeri (Lacerta), Blade Art: Nue (Shidou and Nue), Blade Art: Thunder (Kunai and Kirin).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Parry:</strong> the core verb – parries build Flow for Koo. See the <a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-emma-parry-guide/">parry guide</a>.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Ranged:</strong> the Spring Thunder Crossbow and bows with Fire, Lightning, Poison, Acid and Explosive ammo for boss weaknesses.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Entanglement Overdrive:</strong> a burst state built by parries and dodges, strongest during knockdowns.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Resets:</strong> Mikoto is the reported Amber reset, and v1.0.11 allowed resetting flower-node skills.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm"><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/weapons/">Weapons list →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/weapons/blades/">All 21 blades →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/skills/#emma-skill-tree">Emma skill tree →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/lift-extend-traversal-guide/">Lift and Extend traversal →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/parry-guard-dodge-controls-guide/">Parry, guard and dodge controls →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="koo" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="grid items-start gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_.9fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ember-400">Companion</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold text-ash-50">Koo: Bloom Arts, skills and FP</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ash-300">Koo is the commanded companion in Beast of Reincarnation. His skill trees and Bloom Arts turn the FP created by combat into damage, healing, bindings and elemental pressure while Emma handles the direct sword exchange.</p>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/beast-of-reincarnation-koo-blighted-wolf.webp" alt="Koo, the blighted dog companion, in Beast of Reincarnation" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border border-ash-800 object-cover" />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">Koo's documented skill paths</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-ash-300"><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Pounce:</strong> early attack, trap, healing and utility nodes.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Guard:</strong> status and defensive mod options.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Incantation:</strong> later elemental and status-effect choices.</li><li><strong class="text-ash-100">Bloom Arts:</strong> spend FP on the technique that matches the encounter's visible weakness, then complete the QTE when prompted.</li></ul></div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">How to use Koo without wasting FP</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ash-300">Do not treat every Bloom Art as interchangeable. Read the target's displayed weakness, select the matching technique when the opening is safe, and use the QTE for the strongest reported result. Against a boss, the correct Koo choice is often the one that creates a stagger, bind or healing window rather than the largest unqualified damage number.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-ash-800">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><tbody>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800 first:border-t-0"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Species</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Dog – a stray touched by the blight, himself a Malefact</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Role</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Companion, commanded in combat while you control Emma directly</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Skill achievements</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Giant Tree in Bloom (all skills), Floral Profusion (all flower techniques)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-ash-800"><th scope="row" class="w-2/5 bg-ash-900/60 px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ash-200">Co-op finisher achievement</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ash-300">Koo de Grace (25.6% of Steam players)</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ash-50">Bloom Arts, Nushi skills and story notes</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-ash-300">
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Bloom Arts</strong> are elemental and status attacks named after flowers – Higanbana (fire), Sakura (shock javelin), Dokuzeri, Kiku (Bloom Strike), Erica (Strangle), Numasugi (Skewer).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Nushi skills</strong> are learned from defeated bosses – Rangifer's restraint, Taurus's Charging Botan, Lacerta's Dokuzeri Shower. Both are powered by Flow, built by Emma's parries.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Story:</strong> Koo is central to the story, including a mandatory late encounter with his own Nushi form. Many Mixed Steam reviews still single out Koo as the best part of the game.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ash-100">Cosmetics:</strong> Koo has alternative skins, including a Shiba look. Since v1.0.11 skins and cosmetic items are visible during cutscenes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm"><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/koo-bloom-arts-qte-guide/">Koo Bloom Arts, FP and QTE →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/elements-weakness-stagger-guide/">Elements, weakness and stagger →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/skills/#koo-skill-tree">Koo skill tree →</a><a class="text-ember-400 hover:underline" href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-koo-combat-role/">Koo combat role →</a></p>
    </section>
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ash-50">Story characters</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <WikiSectionCard href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-brad/" label="Ally" title="Brad" description="Pilot of the Cleanse Walker, the ship between regions, and the shop for missed merchant blades." />
      <WikiSectionCard href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-kagura/" label="Ally" title="Kagura" description="The withdrawn colony girl who joins the Cleanse Walker, and how her story mirrors Emma’s." />
      <WikiSectionCard href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-kunai/" label="Rival" title="Kunai" description="The Blightborn swordswoman bonded to Kirin, her Chapter 8 and 12 fights and the Camellia blade." />
      <WikiSectionCard href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-shidou/" label="Boss" title="Shidou" description="The samurai rival bonded to the Nushi Nue and the Mount Hiei fight." />
      <WikiSectionCard href="/guides/beast-of-reincarnation-mikoto/" label="Story" title="Mikoto" description="Met in the Ancient Civilization Zone; the Amber skill reset and his role in the ending." />
    </div>
    <section class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ash-50">How Emma and Koo work together</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ash-300">The official Steam description presents Emma and Koo as a single combat unit: Emma uses sword abilities while the player commands Koo's techniques in a hybrid real-time and turn-based system. The guides linked above keep those roles separate so you can identify whether a problem needs a weapon change, an Emma skill, a Koo Bloom Art or a better parry-to-resource loop.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm"><a class="rounded-lg border border-ash-700 px-4 py-2 text-ember-400 hover:border-ember-500" href="/skills/">Browse Beast of Reincarnation skills and builds</a><a class="rounded-lg border border-ash-700 px-4 py-2 text-ember-400 hover:border-ember-500" href="/guides/gameplay-guide/">Read the combat systems guide</a></div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-500">Skill-path names and priorities are attributed to the cited progression guides; the Emma and Koo combat relationship is described on the <a class="text-ember-400 hover:text-ember-300" href={GAME_FACTS.source} rel="noopener" target="_blank">official Steam page</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
